 "disclosures": [
  "Gate cv-int2-v2: 6 of 7 checks passed on held-out 60 s blocks the detector and tracker were not tuned on. The camera placement was not held out: it was fitted on points Claude read from video frames, some from those same blocks, so the position and lane checks are not independent of that fit. This is agreement with the published NGSIM trajectories, which share this video, and not accuracy.",
  "entering_count_error_share failed: 0.2033 against a limit of <= 0.2. The limit was fixed before the read and was not moved, so what it covers is withheld.",
  "Turning agreement was checked pooled over the held-out blocks, not movement by movement, so no single movement count here has been checked on its own.",
  "Ground positions are approximated through a camera homography, and along-road distances from it are not accepted (ADR-018). Speed is shown because, on vehicles moving at 2 m/s or more, it agreed with the published trajectories within the gate's limit. That agreement is empirical, not a property of the homography, and it is not a calibrated speed measurement.",
  "This run used the optional AGPL-3.0 detector, chosen because it found far more vehicles on this overhead view. The repository's default detector is Apache-2.0.",
  "CairoFlow computer-vision output: boxes come from a detector and tracks from our procedure. It is not ground truth and no value here was measured on the road.",
  "Arms and turns are coarse junction quadrants from a track's first and last points; a track the window cut off has no exit and no turn.",
  "Entering counts hold tracks first seen within 40 px of the image's edge or in the first 0.3 s of the window. The published reference counts every vehicle it holds, so the two definitions differ. 159 other counted tracks began mid-view (E 5, N 97, S 52, W 5). Each is either a restarted track or a queued vehicle the detector first saw moving, so they are left out of entering counts, which can then run low; they stay in the vehicle total and the turns.",
  "Vehicle classes without a detector label are inferred from a rough placed size.",
  "Footage is from Los Angeles in 2005, not Cairo. Image rows from 410 down are the window frame; points there are flagged.",
  "8.0% of track points are interpolated across missed detections and flagged; 5 tracks shorter than 1 s are fragments, kept in the files and left out of the counts.",
  "This window was read for registered held-out gate cv-int2-v2; it may not be used to tune anything.",
  "The published trajectories don't cover every approach in view, so recall can't show misses there. A visual check found stopped vehicles the detector missed."
 ],
